            <div xml:id="d491">

                <pb facs="0497" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/378</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>663. Department’s 532, April 21. Military authorities refuse release Angelo
                    Mazzei claiming if he lost Italian citizenship during his minority, in
                    consequence father’s naturalization, nevertheless, he would have been obliged
                    perform military service in accordance provisions Article 12, Civil Code, which
                    was in force when his class 88 was called.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
